  <entry label="nam_special_normal_00_tetris">
    <text>Block Drop</text>
  </entry>
  <entry label="nam_special_normal_help_00_tetris">
    <text>Summons a falling Tetrimino block that
deals damage on impact. Different block
shapes have unique properties.</text>
  </entry>
  <entry label="nam_special_side_00_tetris">
    <text>T-Spin</text>
  </entry>
  <entry label="nam_special_side_help_00_tetris">
    <text>Transforms into a T-Block and rolls
into foes.</text>
  </entry>
  <entry label="nam_special_upper_00_tetris">
    <text>Hold</text>
  </entry>
  <entry label="nam_special_upper_help_00_tetris">
    <text>Teleports upwards to the inside of a
"Hold" block, briefly floating in place.</text>
  </entry>
  <entry label="nam_special_lower_00_tetris">
    <text>Drop</text>
  </entry>
  <entry label="nam_special_lower_help_00_tetris">
    <text>Rises into the air, allowing for horizontal
movement while held. When released, slams
downwards with force.</text>
  </entry>
  <entry label="nam_final_arts_tetris">
    <text>Block Rain</text>
  </entry>
  <entry label="nam_final_arts_help_tetris">
    <text>Calls down a shower of Tetrimino blocks
to rain across the entire stage, dealing 
massive damage on impact.</text>
  </entry>
  <entry label="nam_peculiar_00_tetris">
    <text>Block Properties</text>
  </entry>
  <entry label="nam_peculiar_help_00_tetris">
    <text>Each Tetrimino block has unique properties:
    ■ I-Block (Line): Spikes opponents downward.
    ■ T-Block: Launch direction depends on which part hits (up/left/right).
    ■ O-Block (Cube): Deals the most damage and knockback.
    ■ S-Block: Launches opponents to the right.
    ■ L-Block: Launches opponents right and upward.
    ■ Z-Block (Reverse S): Launches opponents to the left.
    ■ J-Block (Reverse L): Launches opponents left and upward.</text>
  </entry>
</xmsbt>